  "solution": "**Given**\n\nCompound interest after 2 years = Rs. 1,908\n\nRate of interest = 12% per annum\n\n**Concept:**\n\nCI = P [(1 + r/100)t - 1]\n\n**Solution:**\n\nCI = P [(1 + r/100)t - 1]\n\n⇒ 1908 = P [(1 + 12/100)² - 1]\n\n⇒ 1908 = P [(1 + 3/25)² - 1]\n\n⇒ 1908 = P [(28/25)² - 1]\n\n⇒ 1908 = P [784/625 - 1]\n\n⇒ 1908 = P × 159 / 625\n\n⇒ P = 1908 × 625 / 159\n\n⇒ P = 12 × 625 = Rs. 7500\n\n**Hence, the principal is Rs. 7,500.**",
